["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A goose cups its wings for half a second. In that half second you must know if it is legal, and which bag it fills.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 336\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four goose groups, each with its own limits, 99 percent. Canada and cackling geese, counted together, 10 a day. Snow and Ross&#x27;s geese, counted together, 5 a day, more in MUs 2-4 and 2-5. White fronted geese, the specklebelly, 5 a day. Brant: coast only, MU 2-4, March 1 to 10, 3 a day. Each group has its own dates in each district.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"336\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4 goose groups, 4 sets of limits (99%)</text>\n  <rect x=\"6\" y=\"36\" width=\"190\" height=\"128\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(80 96) scale(0.75)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(140 100) scale(0.5)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"101\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Canada + cackling</text>\n  <text x=\"101\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Counted together</text>\n  <text x=\"101\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 a day</text>\n  <rect x=\"204\" y=\"36\" width=\"190\" height=\"128\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(270 96) scale(0.75)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#e89a8c\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(338 100) scale(0.5)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#e89a8c\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"299\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Snow + Ross&#x27;s</text>\n  <text x=\"299\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Counted together</text>\n  <text x=\"299\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5 a day (2-4, 2-5: more)</text>\n  <rect x=\"6\" y=\"172\" width=\"190\" height=\"128\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(100 232) scale(0.8)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#8c7a66\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#8c7a66\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8c7a66\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#8c7a66\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"101\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">White fronted</text>\n  <text x=\"101\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;Specklebelly&quot;</text>\n  <text x=\"101\" y=\"291\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5 a day</text>\n  <rect x=\"204\" y=\"172\" width=\"190\" height=\"128\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(300 236) scale(0.6)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"299\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Brant</text>\n  <text x=\"299\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Coast only, MU 2-4</text>\n  <text x=\"299\" y=\"291\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">March 1 to 10, 3 a day</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"324\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Each group has its own dates in each district</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>4 goose groups in BC, each with its own limit <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Quick version: <a href=\"#/s/geese\">Geese</a>. This is the deep version, 10 chapters.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this masterclass covers</summary><ul><li>Chapters: <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-01\">1 Meet the animal</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-02\">2 The body</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-03\">3 The senses</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-04\">4 The mind</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-05\">5 The year</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-06\">6 The day</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-07\">7 Where they are</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-08\">8 Sign and tracking</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-09\">9 How to hunt them</a>, <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-10\">10 Shot to table and the rules</a>.</li><li>Main bird: Canada and cackling geese. Snow, Ross's and white fronted geese get their own screens because BC has seasons for them (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds\">Rule Book: migratory birds</a>).</li><li>Brant: one screen here, then the <a href=\"#/s/sea-ducks\">Sea ducks and brant</a> lesson.</li><li>Every chapter ends with Memory hooks and a 5 question quiz. Chapter 10 holds the one page cheat sheet.</li><li>Certainty: 95 to 100% read in the official text. 80 to 94% official source or a study, some reading. 60 to 79% a good secondary source. Tip: opinion.</li><li>Assumption: you hunt with your brother, a 12 gauge with steel shot, a 10 ft boat, a kayak and an ATV (All Terrain Vehicle), from your profile.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Labelled side view of a Canada goose with five marks: black head and neck, white chinstrap, grey brown body, white under the tail, black bill, legs and feet. Sexes look the same, 85 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Canada goose: the 5 marks</text><g transform=\"translate(190 215) scale(2.4 2.4)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"232.0\" y2=\"96.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"232.0,96.0 224.2,97.9 225.7,91.1\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Black head</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">and neck</text><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"262.0\" y2=\"100.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"262.0,100.0 267.9,94.6 269.9,101.3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">White</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">chinstrap</text><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"240.0\" y2=\"205.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"240.0,205.0 246.1,199.9 247.8,206.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Grey brown</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"202\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">body</text><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"105.0\" y2=\"205.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"105.0,205.0 97.2,203.3 101.5,197.8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">White under</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">the tail</text><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"262\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"262.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"200.0,262.0 207.2,258.5 207.2,265.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Black bill,</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">legs and feet</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sexes look the same (85%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Black neck, white chinstrap, white under the tail <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Gander and goose look the same <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/canada-goose.jpg\" alt=\"Canada goose. Black neck and head, white chin strap, brown body. Large, with a long neck.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Canada goose. Black neck and head, white chin strap, brown body. Large, with a long neck. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Joe Ravi, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canada_Goose_(Branta_Canadensis).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every mark and the sizes</summary><ul><li>Black head and neck, a white chinstrap that runs up behind each eye, grey brown body with pale feather edges, black rump and tail, white upper and under tail coverts, black bill, legs and feet (80%, Ducks Unlimited ID).</li><li>Sexes look alike <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Length about 76 to 117 cm (2 ft 6 in to 3 ft 10 in) (80%, Audubon).</li><li>Wingspan about 90 cm to 2 m, by race (80%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li><li>Weight by race: Hinterland Who's Who gives 1.1 kg for the smallest form to 8 kg for the giant form; Ducks Unlimited gives 2.4 to 9 kg (5.3 to 19.8 lb) for the Canada goose races <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. The quick lesson's 1.35 to 5.45 kg covers most birds you will see <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Voice: honks, \"ka lunk\". About 13 different calls have been described (80%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two Canada geese side by side. The gander, the male, is drawn a little bigger, 75 percent. The goose, the female, has the same marks, 85 percent. By fall the young of the year look like adults, 80 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gander, goose, young: same coat</text><g transform=\"translate(110 170) scale(1.75 1.75)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(290 178) scale(1.55 1.55)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><text x=\"110\" y=\"225\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gander (male)</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a bit bigger (75%)</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"225\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Goose (female)</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">same marks (85%)</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"256\" width=\"340\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">By fall the young look like adults (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Same feathers. The gander is a bit bigger <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Watch behaviour: the gander guards and leads <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to tell them apart in the field</summary><ul><li>Ganders (males) are slightly larger than geese (females); otherwise they look alike (75%, Internet Center for Wildlife Damage Management).</li><li>At the nest the gander stands guard, sometimes several hundred metres away (80%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li><li>Before a family flies, the gander's head toss gets them up fastest (80%, Raveling 1969). See <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-04\">Chapter 4</a>.</li><li>Young of the year look like adults by fall <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Goslings stay with their parents a full year <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>In the hand, hunters say young birds have softer, bendier bills and smaller feet (Tip, 60%).</li><li>The law does not care: no sex or age rules for geese in BC (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds\">Rule Book</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Side by side: a Canada goose with a long neck, a bill 4.1 to 5.8 centimetres long and a deep honk, and a smaller cackling goose with a stubby bill 2.8 to 3.8 centimetres long, a short neck and a high yelp, 75 percent. Both count in one bag of 10 a day, 99 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Canada or cackling? Bill, neck, voice</text><g transform=\"translate(110 165) scale(1.9 1.9)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(300 180) scale(1.2 1.2)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><text x=\"110\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Canada</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bill 4.1 to 5.8 cm</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">long neck, deep honk</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cackling</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bill 2.8 to 3.8 cm</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stubby, short neck, yelp</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Both count in one bag: 10 a day (99%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Short neck, stubby bill, high yelp: cackling goose <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Same bag as Canada geese: 10 a day together <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/cackling-and-canada-geese.jpg\" alt=\"Cackling geese with a Canada goose (right). Compare neck and bill.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Cackling geese with a Canada goose (right). Compare neck and bill. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Andy Reago &amp; Chrissy McClarren, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cackling_Goose_(31714908975).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/cackling-goose.jpg\" alt=\"Cackling goose: mallard sized, stubby bill.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Cackling goose: mallard sized, stubby bill. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: VJAnderson, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cackling_Goose_02.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the numbers</summary><ul><li>A <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Cackling goose\">Cackling goose</button> is its own species, split from the Canada goose; it is not a young Canada goose <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Bill: cackling 2.8 to 3.8 cm (1.1 to 1.5 in); Canada 4.1 to 5.8 cm (1.6 to 2.3 in) (75%, Ducks Unlimited).</li><li>Average weight: cackling males about 1.5 kg (1,542 g), females about 0.95 kg (953 g) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>In flight a cackler looks mallard sized with a short neck <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Its call is a higher \"hrooonk\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>In the air the two can be hard or impossible to separate <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. It does not matter for your bag: the law counts \"Canada Geese and Cackling Geese, combined\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Where it lives (75%, Ducks Unlimited)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Western Canada goose</td><td>Resident from BC to Manitoba</td></tr><tr><td>Vancouver Canada goose</td><td>Coastal Alaska to southwest BC</td></tr><tr><td>Dusky and lesser Canada geese</td><td>Alaska and boreal nesters, winter south of BC</td></tr><tr><td>Minima and Taverner's cacklers</td><td>Winter in the Willamette and lower Columbia valleys</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Most BC \"home\" geese are mixed race introductions <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: races, introductions and why it matters</summary><ul><li>Hinterland Who's Who counts 11 races of Canada goose; four former races now make up the cackling goose <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Ducks Unlimited lists the western race (moffitti) as mostly resident from British Columbia to Manitoba, west and south of the Rockies <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The Vancouver race (fulva) breeds from coastal Glacier Bay, Alaska, south to southwest BC <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Dusky geese breed in southern Alaska and winter in the lower Columbia and Willamette valleys; they have declined long term <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Lesser geese (parvipes) breed from boreal Alaska to Nunavut and winter from western Washington to Mexico <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Cackling geese: minima and Taverner's winter in the Willamette and lower Columbia valleys of Oregon and Washington <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. To get there they pass BC (Tip, 65%).</li><li>Okanagan nesting geese are hybrids of several races brought in during the 1960s and 70s; they never learned to migrate (85%, Regional District of Okanagan Similkameen).</li><li>Resident geese in BC towns and valleys are mixed race introductions, often big (85%, quick lesson).</li><li>Why it matters: a September goose is almost always a local bird. Migrants and cacklers mix in from October (Tip, 65%). See <a href=\"#/s/mc-geese-05\">Chapter 5</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three white heads compared. Snow goose: pink bill with a dark grin patch, legal, 99 percent. Ross&#x27;s goose: small stubby bill with a bluish base and no grin, legal, 99 percent. Swan: huge with a black bill, protected, 90 percent. In flight, black wing tips mean snow or Ross&#x27;s goose, 80 percent; all white wings and a longer neck mean swan.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">White birds: name it before you shoot</text><g transform=\"translate(55 90) scale(1.3)\"><path d=\"M-20 60 Q-24 10 0 -4 Q20 -14 30 0 L30 14 Q10 10 4 30 L6 60Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M26 -2 L72 8 L26 16Z\" fill=\"#e89a8c\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M30 9 L52 9\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"2\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(190 95) scale(1.3)\"><path d=\"M-20 60 Q-24 10 0 -4 Q20 -14 30 0 L30 14 Q10 10 4 30 L6 60Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M26 -2 L52 8 L26 16Z\" fill=\"#e89a8c\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M27 2 Q30 0 32 4 Q30 8 27 6Z\" fill=\"#9aa9b8\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"2\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(292 92) scale(1.15)\"><path d=\"M-20 60 Q-24 10 0 -4 Q20 -14 30 0 L30 14 Q10 10 4 30 L6 60Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M26 -2 L78 8 L26 16Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"2\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><text x=\"80\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Snow goose</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">pink bill, dark grin</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">legal (99%)</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ross&#x27;s goose</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stubby, no grin</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">legal (99%)</text><text x=\"335\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Swan</text><text x=\"335\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">huge, black bill</text><text x=\"335\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">protected (90%)</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"252\" width=\"360\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Black wing tips: snow or Ross&#x27;s (80%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"287\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">All white wings, longer neck: swan</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Snow and Ross's count together in one bag <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Grin patch on the bill: snow. Stubby, no grin: Ross's <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/snow-goose.jpg\" alt=\"Snow goose: pink bill with a dark grin patch.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Snow goose: pink bill with a dark grin patch. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Paul Danese, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20250118_snow_goose_barnes_boat_launch_PD000302.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/ross-goose.jpg\" alt=\"Ross's goose: stubby bill, no grin.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Ross's goose: stubby bill, no grin. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Andrew C, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ross%27s_Goose_(Chen_rossii)_(23108182770).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/snow-and-ross-geese.jpg\" alt=\"Snow (left) and Ross's (right).\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Snow (left) and Ross's (right). <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Nomdeploom, CC0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snow_Goose_Ross_Goose_comparison.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-snow-geese-flock.jpg\" alt=\"Dark birds in a snow goose flock are the blue form.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Dark birds in a snow goose flock are the blue form. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Frank Schulenburg, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snow_geese_flying_up_at_Sacramento_National_Wildlife_Refuge.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: marks, weights and limits</summary><ul><li>Snow goose: white with black wing tips, rose pink bill and feet, a dark \"grin patch\" on the bill (80%, Ducks Unlimited).</li><li>Blue morph: white head and neck, grey brown body. Young white birds are greyish with grey pink bills <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Lesser snow goose weights: males 1.9 to 2.8 kg (4.2 to 6.2 lb), females 1.7 to 2.9 kg (3.8 to 6.4 lb) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Ross's goose: smaller, short stubby bill, no grin patch, bluish warty base to the bill on older birds <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Males 1.1 to 2 kg (2.5 to 4.5 lb) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>BC snow geese are the Fraser and Skagit part of the Wrangel Island, Russia, population (85%, Demarchi 2006).</li><li>Limits: District 3 and District 8, 5 a day (15 in possession) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>District 2 (Mission): the federal table says 10 a day, not more than 5 Ross's, possession 30; MUs (Management Units) 2-4 and 2-5 add 5 more snow geese a day (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds\">Rule Book: migratory birds</a>).</li><li>The synopsis page 12 prints 5 a day outside 2-4 and 2-5. The <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2\">Region 2 Rule Book</a> marks this <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> and says take 5 a day in 2-8 to stay safe (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/white-fronted-goose.jpg\" alt=\"White fronted goose: white band at the bill, black bars on the belly.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>White fronted goose: white band at the bill, black bars on the belly. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Frank Schulenburg, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greater_white-fronted_goose_in_flight-1413.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Grey brown, white face band, barred belly: \"specklebelly\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>5 a day in Districts 2, 3 and 8 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: marks, voice and range</summary><ul><li>White patch at the base of a pink orange bill, orange legs, black bars on the belly (75%, quick lesson; Ducks Unlimited).</li><li>Weight about 1.95 to 3.3 kg (70%, search preview of the Cornell Lab guide).</li><li>Voice: a high laughing \"kow kow kow\" from V flocks (80%, quick lesson).</li><li>Two populations, Pacific and mid continent; they travel the Pacific and Central flyways (70%, Ducks Unlimited).</li><li>In the Interior expect passing flocks, not winter birds (Tip, 60%).</li><li>Season limits: 5 a day, 15 in possession, in Districts 2, 3 and 8 (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds\">Rule Book</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Six tiles. Canada goose, legal, 10 a day. Cackling goose, legal, in the same 10. Snow and Ross&#x27;s geese, legal, own limit. White fronted goose, legal, 5 a day. Brant, only MU 2-4 in March. Swans, never, protected. Canada and cackling share one bag; brant is not open at Mission or Kamloops, 99 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Which geese can you shoot in BC?</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"36\" width=\"110\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8f3e0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(70 86) scale(0.7 0.7)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><text x=\"75\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Canada</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 a day*</text><rect x=\"145\" y=\"36\" width=\"110\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8f3e0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(197 92) scale(0.45 0.45)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><text x=\"200\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cackling</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">same 10*</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"36\" width=\"110\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8f3e0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(320 88) scale(0.65 0.65)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-30 -6 L-42 -10 L-34 2Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#e89a8c\"/></g><text x=\"325\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Snow, Ross&#x27;s</text><text x=\"325\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">own limit</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"154\" width=\"110\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8f3e0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(70 206) scale(0.65 0.65)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#8d7b63\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#8d7b63\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8d7b63\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L40 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#f0a060\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><text x=\"75\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">White fronted</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2e7d32\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5 a day</text><rect x=\"145\" y=\"154\" width=\"110\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff4e5\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(197 210) scale(0.45 0.45)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><text x=\"200\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Brant</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">MU 2-4, March</text><rect x=\"270\" y=\"154\" width=\"110\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fdecea\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(320 208) scale(0.7 0.7)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-30 -6 L-42 -10 L-34 2Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><text x=\"325\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Swans</text><text x=\"325\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">never</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"281\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">*Canada and cackling share one bag (99%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Brant: not at Mission or Kamloops (99%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Swans: never. No open season <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Brant: only MU (Management Unit) 2-4, 1 to 10 March <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-trumpeter-swan.jpg\" alt=\"Trumpeter swan: huge, all white, black bill. Protected.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Trumpeter swan: huge, all white, black bill. Protected. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: TRinaud, CC BY 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trumpeter_swan_(Cygnus_buccinator)_2023_2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-tundra-swans-flight.jpg\" alt=\"Tundra swans: white wings, no black tips.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Tundra swans: white wings, no black tips. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service - Midwest Region, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tundra_Swan_(26260317135).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/brant.jpg\" alt=\"Brant: small dark sea goose, white necklace.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Brant: small dark sea goose, white necklace. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Lucwrte, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_Brant_at_Vacation_Isle,_San_Diego.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the look alikes in full</summary><ul><li>A white bird bigger than a goose, with no black wing tips, is a swan. Trumpeter and tundra swans have no open season <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Brant: no open season in Districts 3 and 8 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. In District 2 only in MU 2-4, 1 to 10 March, 3 a day <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Not your bird at Mission or Heffley Creek. Full story: <a href=\"#/s/sea-ducks\">Sea ducks and brant</a>.</li><li>Farm and domestic geese are not wild game. Leave them alone (Tip).</li><li>A dark goose on the coast with no white cheek is a brant, not a Canada goose <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of geese taken in BC each year from the BC Hunter Sample Survey, all goose species together. 2014: 14,369. 2016: 15,539, the peak. 2020: 10,596. 2023: 7,846. 2024: 6,053. Hunters fell from 2,304 in 2016 to 1,345 in 2024. 99 percent as published.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Geese taken in BC each year</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"97.329375\" width=\"24\" height=\"152.670625\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"42\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">14</text><rect x=\"63\" y=\"128.205625\" width=\"24\" height=\"121.794375\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"96\" y=\"84.898125\" width=\"24\" height=\"165.101875\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"108\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">16</text><rect x=\"129\" y=\"128.864375\" width=\"24\" height=\"121.135625\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"162\" y=\"135.961875\" width=\"24\" height=\"114.03812500000001\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"174\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text><rect x=\"195\" y=\"137.130625\" width=\"24\" height=\"112.869375\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"228\" y=\"137.4175\" width=\"24\" height=\"112.58250000000001\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"240\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20</text><rect x=\"261\" y=\"162.758125\" width=\"24\" height=\"87.24187500000001\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"294\" y=\"134.4425\" width=\"24\" height=\"115.5575\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"306\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">22</text><rect x=\"327\" y=\"166.63625\" width=\"24\" height=\"83.36375000000001\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"360\" y=\"185.686875\" width=\"24\" height=\"64.313125\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"372\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">24</text><text x=\"108\" y=\"76.898125\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15,539</text><text x=\"372\" y=\"177.686875\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6,053</text><line x1=\"25\" y1=\"250\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"250\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hunters: 2,304 in 2016, 1,345 in 2024 (99%, survey)</text><text x=\"206\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Estimates, all geese, Hunter Sample Survey</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>BC hunters took 15,539 geese in 2016, 6,053 in 2024 (99%, survey).</li><li>Continent wide, Canada geese boomed since 1950 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the numbers behind it</summary><ul><li>BC Hunter Sample Survey, all geese together: 2016, 2,304 hunters, 15,539 geese. 2024, 1,345 hunters, 6,053 geese (99% as published; these are survey estimates).</li><li>Region 2 geese, 2020 to 2024: 4,249, 4,037, 6,207, 2,629, 2,073 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. MU 2-4 in 2024: 251 hunters, 1,028 geese. MU 2-8 (Mission): 109 hunters, 201 geese <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Region 3, 2020 to 2024: 614, 630, 419, 419, 196 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. MUs 3-27 and 3-28 near Heffley Creek: under 30 estimated goose hunters a year, 0 to 92 geese (99%; small samples, wide error).</li><li>Region 8, 2020 to 2024: 222, 211, 566, 925, 185 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>North America: perhaps 1 million Canada geese in 1950, more than 8 million before the fall hunt now (80%, Hinterland Who's Who). Ducks Unlimited's world estimate: 5.1 to 6.2 million <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Cackling geese: about 3 million, slight recent decline <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Snow geese: about 1 million in 1970, 19 million in 2013, about 14 million in 2019 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Fraser River delta: about 80,000 snow geese wintered in 2004 to 2005; the brackish marsh alone can feed about 17,500 (85%, Demarchi 2006). A peak of about 108,000 was counted in 2016 (70%, Vancouver Sun 2017).</li><li>BC breeding Canada geese more than doubled since 1970 (85%, BC Breeding Bird Atlas, via the quick lesson).</li><li>My reading: fewer hunters, not fewer geese, explains most of the harvest drop (Tip, 60%).</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Memory rhymes (made for this app)</div><ul><li>\"Chinstrap white, neck like night: that is a Canada in sight.\"</li><li>\"Stubby bill, voice up shrill: a cackler, same bag still.\"</li><li>\"Grin on the bill, it is a snow. No grin, small: Ross's, so.\"</li><li>\"All white, no black tips in flight: a swan. Hold tight.\"</li></ul></aside><ul><li>Number trick: <strong>10, 5, 5, 3</strong>. Canada 10, white fronted 5, snow 5 (more in District 2), brant 3 but only MU 2-4 in March <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Old hand's rule (tradition, opinion)</div><p>If you cannot name it, it is not a goose yet. Let it pass and wait for the next one.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Hinterland Who's Who, Ducks Unlimited ID pages, Audubon, BC Hunter Sample Survey, Rule Book. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.hww.ca/en/wildlife/birds/canada-goose.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hinterland Who's Who, Canada goose</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: races, sizes, calls, families, population <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/hunting/waterfowl-id/canada-goose\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, Canada goose ID</a> and <a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/hunting/waterfowl-id/cackling-goose\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">cackling goose ID</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: subspecies, weights, bills, ranges <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/hunting/waterfowl-id/snow-goose\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, snow goose ID</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. <a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/hunting/waterfowl-id/ross-goose\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ross's goose</a> and <a href=\"https://ducks.org/hunting/waterfowl-id/white-fronted-goose\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">white fronted goose</a> from search previews <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.audubon.org/field-guide/bird/canada-goose\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Audubon guide, Canada goose</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://icwdm.org/species/birds/canada-geese/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Internet Center for Wildlife Damage Management, Canada geese</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://rdos.bc.ca/utilities/pest-control-webpages-and-links/goose-management-program\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Regional District of Okanagan Similkameen, goose management</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://canadianfieldnaturalist.ca/index.php/cfn/article/view/290\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Demarchi 2006, Canadian Field Naturalist 120(2)</a>, abstract read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/8425b848-517e-4a20-b26c-6121720382af\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunter Sample Survey Estimates 1976 to 2024</a>, province, region and WMU CSVs downloaded 2026-10-11, species code GOOS (99% as published).</li><li>Vancouver Sun, 10 November 2017, snow goose count, via PressReader search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Rules: <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds\">Rule Book: migratory birds</a> and <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2\">Region 2</a>, checked 2026-10-04 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Full log: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-geese.md</code>.</li></ul></details>"]